# This file follows the Citation File Format (https://citation-file-format.github.io/).
# It describes how to cite LLM-Archive. version/date-released/the DOI were TODO until a formal
# tagged release existed (cadence.yaml's release_publish: Zenodo + DOI, automatic, 90d) — the same
# discipline this project uses for "null until it's true" fields elsewhere (see
# subject_models.yaml). Filled in 2026-09-21 from v0.2, the first release the Zenodo-GitHub
# webhook actually archived (tools/cut_release.py): confirmed live at
# https://zenodo.org/records/22881128 before being copied here, not guessed. The `doi` below is
# the *concept* DOI (10.5281/zenodo.22881127, always resolves to the latest version), not that
# version-specific record DOI — see its own `description`.

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use LLM-Archive's data, code, or methodology, please cite it as below. Cite the specific
  measurement(s) you used by their run_id and protocol_id where possible (see guide/for-researchers.md),
  not just the project as a whole — the project is designed as a growing time series, and a citation
  that names a specific run is falsifiable in a way that a citation of "the project" is not.
type: software
title: "LLM-Archive: a long-running stability archive for commercial language models"
abstract: >-
  A public, append-only measurement archive tracking whether a commercial language model's
  decisions change under equivalent rewordings of the same question, checked monthly against a
  frozen 15-scenario panel per protocol, with a daily self-check against an independent, frozen,
  open-weights reference model. Publishes the noise floor, entropy series, and a worst-case loss
  bound alongside every measurement.
authors:
  - family-names: Kalognomos
    given-names: Michalis
    email: mkalognomos@gmail.com
license:
  - AGPL-3.0-only  # published code
  - CC-BY-4.0      # published data
  - CC-BY-SA-4.0   # published prose
repository-code: "https://github.com/LLM-Archive/llm-archive.github.io"
url: "https://llm-archive.github.io"
version: "v0.2"
date-released: "2026-09-21"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.22881127"
    description: "Zenodo concept DOI — always resolves to the latest version"
keywords:
  - large language models
  - reproducibility
  - decision stability
  - framing effects
  - model evaluation
  - AI transparency
